        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03393-2">
            <title>[8] Superconductivity with a squeeze</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03393-2</link>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><b>Last authors:</b> Michael E. Ziebel</p><p><span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'>Score 8/10</span> <b>B_IMPORTANT_CONDMAT</b></p><p><b>Why:</b> Heavy-fermion superconductivity in van der Waals material, relevant to Kondo and correlated systems.</p><p><b>Tags:</b> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#superconductivity</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#heavyfermion</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#vanderWaals</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#Kondo</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#stronglycorrelated</span></p><p><img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41567-026-03393-2/MediaObjects/41567_2026_3393_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /></p><hr/><p><b>Abstract:</b> Heavy-fermion superconductivity has now been observed under pressure in the van der Waals metal CeSiI. This material will provide a new platform for studying the interplay of dimensionality and Kondo physics.</p>]]></content:encoded>
            <dc:title>[8] Superconductivity with a squeeze</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Michael E. Ziebel</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/s41567-026-03393-2</dc:identifier>
            <dc:source>Nature Physics, Published online: 2026-07-28; | doi:10.1038/s41567-026-03393-2</dc:source>
            <dc:date>2026-07-28</dc:date>
            <prism:publicationName>Nature Physics</prism:publicationName>
            <prism:doi>10.1038/s41567-026-03393-2</prism:doi>
            <prism:url>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41567-026-03393-2</prism:url>
        <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Last authors:&lt;/b&gt; Michael E. Ziebel&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'&gt;Score 8/10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;b&gt;B_IMPORTANT_CONDMAT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why:&lt;/b&gt; Heavy-fermion superconductivity in van der Waals material, relevant to Kondo and correlated systems.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tags:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#superconductivity&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#heavyfermion&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#vanderWaals&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#Kondo&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#stronglycorrelated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://media.springernature.com/m685/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41567-026-03393-2/MediaObjects/41567_2026_3393_Fig1_HTML.png' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Abstract:&lt;/b&gt; Heavy-fermion superconductivity has now been observed under pressure in the van der Waals metal CeSiI. This material will provide a new platform for studying the interplay of dimensionality and Kondo physics.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item>
    
